WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.024
Why AI increasingly

00:00:01.836 --> 00:00:02.543
wants to run

00:00:02.355 --> 00:00:03.262
on your laptop

00:00:03.798 --> 00:00:05.484
Pete Warden co-creator

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:06.463
of Moonshine Voice

00:00:06.322 --> 00:00:07.453
and a longtime

00:00:07.277 --> 00:00:08.632
deep learning engineer

00:00:08.845 --> 00:00:10.224
explains why AI

00:00:10.036 --> 00:00:10.991
wants to run

00:00:10.803 --> 00:00:11.911
locally rather than

00:00:11.723 --> 00:00:12.571
in the cloud

00:00:13.102 --> 00:00:14.021
He covers the

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:15.118
fast progress of

00:00:14.977 --> 00:00:16.109
open-weight models

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:16.863
and what it

00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:17.500
takes to run

00:00:17.312 --> 00:00:18.738
AI on laptops

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.682
and in browsers

00:00:19.821 --> 00:00:21.424
Apple's M5 Studio

00:00:21.236 --> 00:00:23.075
can have 256

00:00:22.887 --> 00:00:24.172
gigabytes of memory

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.054
Plus how low-latency

00:00:25.866 --> 00:00:27.033
speech models could

00:00:26.844 --> 00:00:27.646
make voice a

00:00:27.458 --> 00:00:28.695
natural interface

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:29.875
and hardware that

00:00:29.686 --> 00:00:31.349
could challenge GPUs

00:00:31.878 --> 00:00:32.892
Full story on

00:00:32.703 --> 00:00:33.599
the dashboard
